  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Zornia latifolia § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zornia_latifolia#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1301264128,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "■ Forage\nThis legume is a nutritious and palatable forage for livestock. It can be grown as a companion plant to grasses such as Andropogon gayanus and Brachiaria decumbens.\n\n■ Hallucinogen and adulteration\nA common component of many synthetic cannabis mixtures producing hallucinogenic effects, such as the street drug, 'Spice', though these mixtures effects are caused by synthetic cannaboids, Zornia latifolia may have cannabis-like effects. It may be adulterated by a different Fabaceae plant, Stylosanthes guianensis, which is phytochemically different from Zornia latifolia. The flavones genistein, apigenin and syzalterin may explain the cannabis-like effects of Zornia latifolia.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
